  <h3 style="margin-top: 40px;">University Policies</h3>
  <p><strong>Dropping and Adding</strong></p>
  <p>Students are responsible for understanding the policies and procedures about add/drop, grade forgiveness, etc. Refer to the current semester's <span data-field="catalog_link">{{ catalog_link }}</span> section at <span data-field="catalog_url">{{ catalog_url }}</span>. Add/drop deadlines can be found on the current academic year calendars document on the <span data-field="academic_calendar_link">{{ academic_calendar_link }}</span> webpage at <span data-field="academic_calendar_url">{{ academic_calendar_url }}</span>. The <span data-field="late_drop_policy_link">{{ late_drop_policy_link }}</span> is available at <span data-field="late_drop_policy_url">{{ late_drop_policy_url }}</span>. Students should be aware of the current deadlines and penalties for dropping classes.</p>

  <p><strong>Consent for Recording of Class and Public Sharing of Instructor Material</strong></p>
  <p>University Policy S12-7, <span data-field="policy_url">{{ policy_url }}</span>, requires students to obtain instructor's permission to record the course.</p>

  <ul>
    <li>"Common courtesy and professional behavior dictate that you notify someone when you are recording him/her. You must obtain the instructor's permission to make audio or video recordings in this class. Such permission allows the recordings to be used for your private, study purposes only. The recordings are the intellectual property of the instructor; you have not been given any rights to reproduce or distribute the material."</li>
    <li>"It is suggested that the green sheet include the instructor's process for granting permission, whether in writing or orally and whether for the whole semester or on a class by class basis."</li>
    <li>"In classes where active participation of students or guests may be on the recording, permission of those students or guests should be obtained as well."</li>
    <li>"Course material developed by the instructor is the intellectual property of the instructor and cannot be shared publicly without his/her approval. You may not publicly share or upload instructor generated material for this course such as exam questions, lecture notes, or homework solutions without instructor consent."</li>
  </ul>

  <h4 style="margin-top: 30px;">Academic integrity</h4>
  <p>Your commitment as a student to learning is evidenced by your enrollment at San Jose State University. The <span data-field="university_academic_integrity_policy_link">{{ university_academic_integrity_policy_link }}</span> at <span data-field="university_academic_integrity_policy_url">{{ university_academic_integrity_policy_url }}</span> requires you to be honest in all your academic course work. Faculty members are required to report all infractions to the office of Student Conduct and Ethical Development. The <span data-field="student_conduct_link">{{ student_conduct_link }}</span> website is available at <span data-field="student_conduct_url">{{ student_conduct_url }}</span>.</p>
  <p>Instances of academic dishonesty will not be tolerated. Cheating on exams or plagiarism (presenting the work of another as your own, or the use of another person's ideas without giving proper credit) will result in a failing grade and sanctions by the University. For this class, all assignments are to be completed by the</p>
  <p><span data-field="submission_date">{{ submission_date }}</span></p>
